{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Synthetic data as a dataset operation (ruling 10). Two transforms, two addresses: render_dialect (procedural, runs in the service - the serving dialect keeps one home) and distill_why (model-driven, harvest H3b, runs behind the frontier arm): for up to limit source rows per deliberate run (1-25, the explicit spend cap; a done-set makes re-runs spend only on new rows), assembles an H2 coding context, asks why the change was made and what it teaches, then deposits a hysteresis-guarded claim on the subject control (patch rows) and one QA conversation row into the out stream (sft) via dataset_feed. Every row carries generator, source pin, and row hash - the generator is a provenance tag, never a branch.","import":"use ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse flowlang::flowlang::system::time::time;\nuse ndata::data::Data;\nuse crate::agent::model::dataset_feed::dataset_feed;\nuse crate::agent::llm::ask_llm::ask_llm;\nuse crate::agent::archivist::adjudicate::adjudicate;","params":[{"desc":"Source dataset.","name":"name","type":"String"},{"desc":"Name for the derived dataset - lineage records derived:<transform>:<source>.","name":"out_name","type":"String"},{"desc":"This branch ships render_dialect: curriculum JSONL rows rendered to training docs by the service's own render_sample, so the dialect keeps one home.","name":"transform","type":"String"},{"desc":"distill_why's explicit spend cap: how many source rows may be distilled this run (1-25; each costs one frontier call). The done-set makes re-runs spend only on rows not yet distilled. render_dialect ignores it.","name":"limit","type":"Integer"}],"returntype":"JSONObject","type":"rust"},"id":"oopiwl1a01784a023z1","readers":[],"time":1787143683675,"username":"system","writers":[]}